{
  "about": "One spelling per meaning, through the shipped schema before any study data is read (SCHEMA-15, EXPR-5, LAYER-4, LAYER-12): a long form that holds only what its shorthand holds restates it and is refused where it is written, a structured source holding only its variable restates the bare read wherever a source is written, unless its text is no name the grammar reads (FORMULA-2), a long form that adds a field keeps its meaning, a list field takes a list even for one value, and every layer is held to the shorthand it writes; a retired temporal verb names the operation and declared type that replace it. Moved from declaration_one_spelling.rs and declaration_migration_hints.rs, which prepared each specification through shipped_schema::prepare and read its findings, and from the refusal halves and admitted forms of declaration_v1_lowering.rs, which prepared it through the document front end and read its findings before they were projected (FUNC-6, LOOKUP-3, WINDOW-5, TIME-10). A refusal runs check, the public static check, and prepare_specification, the preparation those tests called, which report the same complete rows; an admitted form runs prepare_specification alone, since those tests claimed only that the preparation admits it, not that the compiled specification checks clean. A finding in a layer's own document names that layer as source and the entry as entry, each as the study path the engine spells (LAYER-4, LAYER-12): the entry's own findings name spec.yaml or entry.yaml as both, and a parent's names parent.yaml as its source. A finding of the front end over the composed specification (FUNC-6, LOOKUP-3, WINDOW-5) names neither: its row holds exactly the context its test compared. The tests of one_spelling compared each finding whole, or its condition, spec paths and one context key; those of migration_hints its condition, spec path, operation and hint; and those of v1_lowering each finding's code, which gives its phase, condition and rule, its path and its context, beside which a layer's finding, the long form of a check that declares no field, names its source and entry. The documents: column writes V's derivation as DERIVATION, which each case replaces; entry declares parent.yaml, and parent writes V's derivation as DERIVATION; retired_verb writes ID's derivation operation as VERB; one_layer is a one-layer specification over SRC and EX whose added column is COLUMN, output after ID as OUTPUT.",
  "documents": {
    "column": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ndomain: TEST\nkeys: [ID]\nbase: DM\noutput: {path: out.csv, columns: [ID, V]}\ninput: {DM: dm.csv, EX: ex.csv}\ncolumns:\n  - {name: ID, type: str, derivation: DM.ID}\n  - name: V\n    type: int\n    derivation: DERIVATION\n",
    "entry": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ndomain: TEST\nkeys: [ID]\nbase: DM\noutput: {path: out.csv, columns: [ID, V]}\nparent: parent.yaml\n",
    "parent": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ninput: {DM: dm.csv, EX: ex.csv}\ncolumns:\n  - {name: ID, type: str, derivation: DM.ID}\n  - {name: V, type: int, derivation: DERIVATION}\n",
    "retired_verb": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ndomain: TEST\nkeys: [ID]\ninput: {SRC: missing.csv}\noutput: {path: out.csv, columns: [ID]}\ncolumns:\n  - name: ID\n    type: str\n    derivation: {VERB: {source: SRC.VALUE}}\n",
    "one_layer": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ndomain: T\nkeys: [ID]\ninput: {SRC: src.csv, EX: ex.csv}\nbase: SRC\noutput: {path: out.csv, columns: [ID, OUTPUT]}\ncolumns:\n  - {name: ID, type: int, derivation: SRC.ID}\n  - COLUMN\n"
  },
